  "label": "Early career and graduate",
  "_about": "Lou, 22/10/2026: list entry-level roles for people without medical sales experience who have a proven track record in their own industry. A role is tagged early career when its TITLE says so (graduate, trainee, associate, junior, assistant, sales development representative, inside sales) alongside a sales, commercial, account, marketing or clinical-specialist word. The tag is about the title only. The posting itself says whether experience is required, so the page tells members to read it. Roles already in another category keep that category and carry the tag as well; a tagged role that fits no other category is listed under this one.",
  "patterns": [
   "\\b(graduate|early[- ]careers?|trainee|apprentice(ship)?|entry[- ]level|junior|associate)\\b.*\\b(sales|commercial|account|territory|business development|marketing|market access|tender|bids?|clinical (specialist|sales|support|advis\\w*|educat\\w*)|product (specialist|marketing|manager|executive)|customer success)\\b",
